cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "port: Positive-semi-definiteness Of Rounded correlation Tables"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hussey
    given-names: Ian
    email: ian.hussey@unibe.ch
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8906-7559"
abstract: >-
  Forensic meta-science tools for auditing reported correlation matrices.
  Published correlations are rounded, so each true value lies somewhere within a
  small range around the printed number. The package asks whether any valid
  correlation matrix -- one that is positive semidefinite -- can lie within all
  of those ranges at once. When none can, the reported table cannot have arisen
  as a single complete set of Pearson correlations.
keywords:
  - meta-science
  - error detection
  - correlation matrices
  - positive semidefinite
  - R
